    <bpmn:process id="W_W5508" name="W5508. Fringe Benefits Tax (FBT) Determination, Valuation &amp; Quarterly BIR Form 1605 Filing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly FBT computation and filing cycle (15 days after quarter close); benefit-plan or de-minimis-threshold changes at C&amp;B; new fringe-benefit source activation (housing allocation, vehicle assignment, loan issuance)
Frequency: Continuous benefit-event accrual; quarterly filing per entity
Volume: 5 entities × 4 quarters = 20 BIR 1605 filings/year; ~40–120 FBT-liable benefit instances per quarter chain-wide (managerial/supervisory recipients only — housing allocations, executive vehicle personal-use, club memberships, below-market loans, officer-only medical)
Owner: Tax Accountant
Participants: Tax Accountant, C&amp;B Manager, Payroll Manager, HRIS Analyst, Controller (computation review), CFO (filing approval), external tax advisor (interpretation)
Source: workflow W5508 — Fringe Benefits Tax (FBT) Determination, Valuation &amp; Quarterly BIR Form 1605 Filing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5508_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5508_Lane1" name="Tax Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5508_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5508_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5508_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5508_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5508_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5508_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5508_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5508_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5508_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5508_Lane3" name="C&amp;B Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5508_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5508_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5508_Start5" name="Quarterly FBT computation and filing cycle (15 days after quarter close); benefit-plan or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5508_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5508_Task6" name="Benefit-source identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Benefit-source identification: Tax Accountant and C&amp;B Manager maintain the fringe-benefit source register fed from HRIS and the C&amp;B benefit master (W3313/W3316): employer-provided housing incl. dormitory allocations to managerial residents (VS-144), vehicle personal-use share from fleet assignment logs and telematics (VS-06), officer-only HMO/medical beyond the universal plan (W3313), educational assistance, club memberships, below-market employee loans (imputed interest on W76 loan issuances), and employee-discount patterns beyond policy (W5B.12 limits); each source carries a valuation method, rank-eligibility flag, and entity attribution
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant / C&amp;B Manager
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: Quarterly refresh, 2–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5508_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5508_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5508_Task7" name="Rank and exclusion test">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Rank and exclusion test: system classifies each benefit event: (a) recipient rank — FBT applies only to managerial/supervisory employees; benefits furnished to the general rank-and-file population are instead taxable compensation routed to W2764; (b) exclusion screening — de minimis benefits within the BIR threshold schedule (RR 3-98 as updated by RR 5-2018: monetized unused leave within limits, rice subsidy, uniforms, rank-and-file medical assistance within caps), mandatory contributions, and benefits required for the employer&#x27;s convenience / furnished on the necessity of the business (e.g., worksite housing where residency is required) are excluded with documented rationale
Responsible (R): System / Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: Automated + 1–2 hours/quarter review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5508_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5508_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5508_Task8" name="Valuation per NIRC §33 rules">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Valuation per NIRC §33 rules: housing at fair rental value; vehicles at depreciation plus operating costs × personal-use share (telematics/logbook evidence); loans at imputed interest using the prescribed rate × forgone spread; other benefits at acquisition cost; Tax Accountant overrides system values where evidence dictates (e.g., co-occupied housing pro-ration)
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5508_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5508_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5508_Task9" name="Gross-up computation and aggregation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Gross-up computation and aggregation: system computes the grossed-up monetary value (monetary value ÷ (1 − 35%)) and FBT thereon at 35%, aggregated per employee, per benefit type, per entity; FBT is a final tax — the benefit is excluded from the employee&#x27;s taxable compensation so no W2764 double-count (BIR 2316 coordination at year-end via W2765)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5508_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5508_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5508_Task10" name="Monthly accrual and reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly accrual and reconciliation: month-end close posts the FBT accrual (Dr. Fringe Benefits Tax Expense / Cr. FBT Payable) per the W9A tax-provision step; Tax Accountant reconciles the benefit-event register to the GL accrual and to payroll/payslip exclusion trails; variances investigated before filing
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant / Chief Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 30–45 min/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5508_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5508_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5508_Task11" name="Quarterly BIR 1605 filing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly BIR 1605 filing: Tax Accountant generates BIR Form 1605 per entity from the FBT register, reviews against the accrual, and files via eFPS within 15 days following quarter close (due-date governance per the W2776 tax calendar); payment via e-Payment rails per W2755; BIR confirmation and PRN archived in the tax evidence repository
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 hours/entity/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5508_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5508_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5508_Task12" name="Evidence, audit defense and employee-facing consistency">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Evidence, audit defense and employee-facing consistency: FBT register, valuation evidence (telematics extracts, rental appraisals, loan amortization schedules), exclusion rationale memos, and filed 1605s retained 10 years per BIR rules; register excerpt feeds BIR audit response (W2773) and the annual information-return ecosystem (W2765); employee-side: FBT-covered benefits flagged in the HRIS so they neither appear as taxable compensation on 2316s nor are double-reported
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: 30 min/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5508_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5508_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5508_Task13" name="Annual benefit-design review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Annual benefit-design review: C&amp;B Manager and Tax Accountant review benefit-plan changes for FBT efficiency (structure vs cash-equivalent, de-minimis headroom under updated BIR issuances, rank-population design that keeps benefits universal where intended), feeding the W3320 benefits cost model, the W2776 tax-risk register, and next year&#x27;s plan design (W3313 renewal)
Responsible (R): C&amp;B Manager / Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): CHRO / CFO
Duration: Annual, 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5508_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5508_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5508_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5508_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5508_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-467 (ensure controlled execution — Withholding Tax (EWT/CWT) &amp; Form 2307 Management (PA-79.2).) | - operational: exclusion rationale memos per benefit type; telematics/appraisal valuation evidence attached before computation; three-way register/GL/payroll reconciliation before each quarterly filing; 10-year evidence retention feeding W2773 audit defense
Owner: Tax Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5508_Assoc16" sourceRef="W5508_Annotation15" targetRef="W5508_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5508_Flow17" sourceRef="W5508_Start5" targetRef="W5508_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5508_Flow18" sourceRef="W5508_Task6" targetRef="W5508_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5508_Flow19" sourceRef="W5508_Task7" targetRef="W5508_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5508_Flow20" sourceRef="W5508_Task8" targetRef="W5508_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5508_Flow21" sourceRef="W5508_Task9" targetRef="W5508_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5508_Flow22" sourceRef="W5508_Task10" targetRef="W5508_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5508_Flow23" sourceRef="W5508_Task11" targetRef="W5508_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5508_Flow24" sourceRef="W5508_Task12" targetRef="W5508_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5508_Flow25" sourceRef="W5508_Task13" targetRef="W5508_End14" />
    </bpmn:process>
