        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W5508_Flow25_di" bpmnElement="W5508_Flow25"><di:waypoint x="2050" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="2100" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W5508_Assoc16_di" bpmnElement="W5508_Assoc16"><di:waypoint x="340" y="630" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W5533" name="W5533. BIR Form 2316 Annual Issuance, Employee Acknowledgment &amp; Certificate Lifecycle" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Calendar year-end close (the W9A/W10 year-end payroll cycle); the January 31 BIR deadline for furnishing 2316 to employees; the February 28 deadline for the related 1604C/alphalist filing (W2765); an employee separation (W43/W643) requiring an interim certificate; an employee request for a replacement or corrected certificate; or a BIR/labor examination evidence request (W77)
Frequency: Annual issuance cycle with per-separation interim issuances; event-driven replacements and corrections
Volume: ~6,925 active employees furnished annually across the multi-entity payroll (W816 consolidation scope, 5 entities) + ~1,400–1,600 separated employees/year receiving separation 2316s; acknowledgment tracking to a ≥ 98% completion gate per entity; ~50–100 replacement/correction requests/year
Owner: Tax Manager
Participants: Payroll Specialist, HR Shared Services (W3334-class issuance/verification requests), HR Technology Manager (ESS distribution per W3330), Store/DC HR Administrators (printed-copy distribution), Controller, External Audit Team, BIR (deadline regime and examination requests), Employees (recipients)
Source: workflow W5533 — BIR Form 2316 Annual Issuance, Employee Acknowledgment &amp; Certificate Lifecycle</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5533_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5533_Lane1" name="Payroll Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5533_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5533_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5533_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5533_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5533_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5533_Lane2" name="HR Technology Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5533_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5533_Lane3" name="Tax Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5533_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5533_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5533_Start5" name="Calendar year-end close (the W9A/W10 year-end payroll cycle); the January 31 BIR deadline…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5533_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5533_Task6" name="Year-end data assembly &amp; validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Year-end data assembly &amp; validation: per entity, assemble annual gross compensation and withholding per employee from the W10/W816 payroll runs — 13th-month exempt excess (W1416/W1384), taxable benefits, prior-employer income declared by mid-year hires; reconcile per-employee totals to the W2764 monthly 1601C remittances and pre-validate against the W2765 1604C/alphalist before any certificate is issued
Responsible (R): Payroll Specialist
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours per entity per year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5533_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5533_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5533_Task7" name="Certificate generation &amp; QC">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Certificate generation &amp; QC: generate BIR Form 2316 per employee from the payroll/tax module (the W90.8 certificate-generation capability, BIR December format); QC-sample per entity (marginal tax rates, exempt 13th-month treatment, net compensation figure, TIN validity against the W292 employee master) and correct at source before distribution
Responsible (R): Payroll Specialist
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: 6–8 hours per year (generation) + QC</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5533_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5533_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5533_Task8" name="Distribution &amp; acknowledgment tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Distribution &amp; acknowledgment tracking: distribute via ESS download (the W3330 portal tax-document capability) with e-acknowledgment capture; run printed-copy distribution with signed receipt logs for non-ESS populations (store/DC staff) administered by store HR; track per-entity acknowledgment completion daily in January and escalate laggard sites at T-7 days before the January 31 deadline
Responsible (R): HR Technology Manager / Store HR Administrators
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: ~40–60 hours/year (store distribution effort dominates: ~15–20 min/store × ~200 stores)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5533_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5533_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5533_Task9" name="Separation &amp; interim issuance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Separation &amp; interim issuance: issue the 2316 upon separation as a W43 clearance-checklist item gated in the W643 final-pay release; issue interim certificates on employee request for financing, visa or loan purposes (the W2972 financing-desk evidence demand) within 2 business days
Responsible (R): Payroll Specialist / HR Shared Services
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: ~0.3 h per separation × ~1,400–1,600/year; per-request otherwise</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5533_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5533_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5533_Task10" name="Corrections &amp; replacements">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Corrections &amp; replacements: process corrected certificates where under/over-withholding is identified — feed the correction back to W2764 adjustments (refund or deficiency handling) and reissue; log every replacement with a reason code for the annual quality review
Responsible (R): Payroll Specialist
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: per request; ~50–100 requests/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5533_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5533_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5533_Task11" name="Deadline evidence &amp; audit support">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Deadline evidence &amp; audit support: archive the issuance evidence pack (generation logs, acknowledgment register, ESS download logs, printed-copy receipt sign-offs, separation-issue records) per the W256/W2977 retention schedule; fold into the W351/W95 audit package and the BIR-examination evidence per W77 — the 2316 file is the standard first document request in a compensation-tax examination
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: ~12 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5533_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5533_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5533_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5533_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5533_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-467 (ensure controlled execution — Withholding Tax (EWT/CWT) &amp; Form 2307 Management (PA-79.2).) | - operational: annual issuance cannot close per entity until the 2316-to-1604C reconciliation is signed off by the Tax Manager | - operational: separation 2316 issuance is a W643 final-pay release checklist gate; overrides require Payroll Manager approval and are logged
Owner: Tax Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5533_Assoc14" sourceRef="W5533_Annotation13" targetRef="W5533_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5533_Flow15" sourceRef="W5533_Start5" targetRef="W5533_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5533_Flow16" sourceRef="W5533_Task6" targetRef="W5533_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5533_Flow17" sourceRef="W5533_Task7" targetRef="W5533_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5533_Flow18" sourceRef="W5533_Task8" targetRef="W5533_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5533_Flow19" sourceRef="W5533_Task9" targetRef="W5533_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5533_Flow20" sourceRef="W5533_Task10" targetRef="W5533_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5533_Flow21" sourceRef="W5533_Task11" targetRef="W5533_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
